  There are two blues: light blue and dark blue.  I've had trouble
with other roguelikes (not Nethack that I can recall) with dark blue
or dark gray looking almost black, due to monitor burnout.  If you
know how to change the terminal colors, try that --- or hope somebody
else knows how.
  I've also seen the terminal colors (especially the brown of jackals
and doors) change when I do 'mode con:lines=25' (the WinXP equivalent
of the old 'mode co80') or Alt-Enter, or enter and exit old DOS programs.
Also the character glyph tables, noticeably the backquote ` goes from
a thick straight diagonal line to a hooked backquote sometimes.  This
is just Microsoft Windows being buggy, I think.  You might play with
these things and see if they fix your blue problem, though, anyway.

  Also, try turning up the brightness on your monitor.  If there are
really fountains there, but really dark, you could always try getting
a new monitor. ;-)

